## 5. Performance & Scaling Details

```
LATENCY BUDGET (100ms requirement)
───────────────────────────────────
Client keypress → Local CRDT apply:     ~0ms  (synchronous)
Local render:                           ~16ms (next frame)
Network to server (p50):                ~20ms
Server apply + broadcast:               ~5ms  
Network to other clients:               ~20ms
Remote client render:                   ~16ms
──────────────────────────────────────────────
Total perceived latency:                ~61ms ✓ (under 100ms)

The local-first approach is key:
User sees their OWN edits at 0ms latency
Other users see changes in 50-70ms
```

```
CAPACITY PLANNING
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
WebSocket Servers (8 core, 32GB RAM):
  - Each handles 10,000 connections safely
  - 500K users / 10K = 50 servers needed (peak)
  - Normal load: ~5-10 servers

Memory per room:
  - Y.Doc for 100KB document: ~2MB
  - 10,000 rooms in memory: ~20GB
  - Spread across 50 servers: ~400MB/server ✓

Redis:
  - 10,000 active docs × 200KB avg: ~2GB
  - Pub/sub throughput: ~100MB/s (easily handled)
  - Cluster: 3 shards × 16GB = 48GB capacity

PostgreSQL:
  - 1M ops/day × 200 bytes = 200MB/day
  - With partitioning by month: manageable
  - Read replicas for version history queries

S3 snapshots:
  - 10,000 docs × 500KB avg: ~5GB
  - Cost: ~$0.15/month
```

